repository-code: "https://github.com/sigilante/data-substrates-2027"
abstract: >-
  A classified census of state migrations in the Urbit personal server,
  reconstructed from public Git history (2013–2026): 111 migration steps in
  five system components (Ames, Gall, Clay, Dojo, Hood) and 38 migration rows
  in six userspace agents. Each step carries a kind, flags, and a sequence of
  operators drawn from Cambria's lens operators plus five additions, with the
  labels of two independent LLM coders and the author's adjudication. Includes
  version-landing histories, network protocol-version changes, the review
  interface with per-step diffs, and the scripts that generate every table
  and figure in the accompanying paper. Data are CC BY 4.0; code is MIT.
keywords:
  - schema evolution
  - state migration
  - Urbit
  - malleable systems
  - local-first software
  - edit lenses
  - Cambria
  - software archaeology
